{"type":"standard","title":"Pat Fallon","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Pat Fallon</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q16196923","titles":{"canonical":"Pat_Fallon","normalized":"Pat Fallon","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Pat Fallon</span></span>"},"pageid":42261851,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/PatFallon118th.jpg/330px-PatFallon118th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/PatFallon118th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1000,"height":1250},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1361100469","tid":"23ab8cd9-70b6-11f1-a7df-abe04e63a8e9","timestamp":"2026-06-25T16:51:41Z","description":"American businessman and politician (born 1967)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pat_Fallon","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pat_Fallon?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pat_Fallon?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Pat_Fallon"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pat_Fallon","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Pat_Fallon","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pat_Fallon?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Pat_Fallon"}},"extract":"Patrick Edward Fallon is an American businessman and politician. A member of the Republican Party, he has been the U.S. representative for Texas's 4th congressional district since 2021. Fallon was also a member of the Texas House of Representatives for the 106th district from 2013 to 2019 and represented the 30th district of the Texas Senate from 2019 to 2021.","extract_html":"<p><b>Patrick Edward Fallon</b> is an American businessman and politician. A member of the Republican Party, he has been the U.S. representative for Texas's 4th congressional district since 2021. Fallon was also a member of the Texas House of Representatives for the 106th district from 2013 to 2019 and represented the 30th district of the Texas Senate from 2019 to 2021.</p>"}